              "falseColor": false,
              "notes": "The colour of a 4,416 K blackbody, Gaia DR3's photometric temperature. The darkening toward the edge is Patel & Espinoza (2022)'s fit to TESS transits (600–1000 nm): the edge is 45% as bright as the centre, anywhere from about 25 to 80% within their uncertainty. The star is magnetically active (Esposito et al. 2017), so it has spots, but no map of them exists. Its axis follows the planet's orbit, as measured."
